    {
      "id": "pByiISYq",
      "type": "text",
      "x": -469.94568840729437,
      "y": 1213.7420936152741,
      "width": 830.259521484375,
      "height": 250,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b0T",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 216587315,
      "version": 518,
      "versionNonce": 1193945715,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1789279516580,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "3. Rate Limiting ->\n   a. Manage Burst Limit-> means max no of concurent request that api gateway\n     can handle before it returns 413 (too many request )\n    b. API Throttling ->  Limit the no of request from a particualr api itself . BLock \n    api request once they crossed certain limit \n    c. Ipbased blocking \n    d.API queries -> HOld request to an api whihc cant be processed immediatley . \n    help us to handle tundering herd issue . \n\n ",
      "rawText": "3. Rate Limiting ->\n   a. Manage Burst Limit-> means max no of concurent request that api gateway\n     can handle before it returns 413 (too many request )\n    b. API Throttling ->  Limit the no of request from a particualr api itself . BLock \n    api request once they crossed certain limit \n    c. Ipbased blocking \n    d.API queries -> HOld request to an api whihc cant be processed immediatley . \n    help us to handle tundering herd issue . \n\n ",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "3. Rate Limiting ->\n   a. Manage Burst Limit-> means max no of concurent request that api gateway\n     can handle before it returns 413 (too many request )\n    b. API Throttling ->  Limit the no of request from a particualr api itself . BLock \n    api request once they crossed certain limit \n    c. Ipbased blocking \n    d.API queries -> HOld request to an api whihc cant be processed immediatley . \n    help us to handle tundering herd issue . \n\n ",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "xREbVxuL",
      "type": "text",
      "x": -480.8145309881263,
      "y": 1471.400450701543,
      "width": 827.2595825195312,
      "height": 650,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b0U",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 409259261,
      "version": 784,
      "versionNonce": 2125462301,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1789285622148,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "4. Service Discovery -> Means getting the Instances of the services instances .\n    ie getting a list of the ip addreess \n    \n    How does Service Discovery get all this data ?\n    Approaches \n        a.Service ping the health checks of the service to see all the active instances\n        b. Active instance on the scale up or down give the new ip adress  \n\n\n\nInterview QUESTION \n\nDOES API GATEWAY IS A SINGLE POINT OF FAILURE ?????????\n \nAnseer below \n We have regions and in regions we have data center as you can see\n Az1 , Az2 ..... AZn zone . \n  \n DNS depenceing on the request will distribute request to near by \n regions \n\n\n\n \n\n ",
      "rawText": "4. Service Discovery -> Means getting the Instances of the services instances .\n    ie getting a list of the ip addreess \n    \n    How does Service Discovery get all this data ?\n    Approaches \n        a.Service ping the health checks of the service to see all the active instances\n        b. Active instance on the scale up or down give the new ip adress  \n\n\n\nInterview QUESTION \n\nDOES API GATEWAY IS A SINGLE POINT OF FAILURE ?????????\n \nAnseer below \n We have regions and in regions we have data center as you can see\n Az1 , Az2 ..... AZn zone . \n  \n DNS depenceing on the request will distribute request to near by \n regions \n\n\n\n \n\n ",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "4. Service Discovery -> Means getting the Instances of the services instances .\n    ie getting a list of the ip addreess \n    \n    How does Service Discovery get all this data ?\n    Approaches \n        a.Service ping the health checks of the service to see all the active instances\n        b. Active instance on the scale up or down give the new ip adress  \n\n\n\nInterview QUESTION \n\nDOES API GATEWAY IS A SINGLE POINT OF FAILURE ?????????\n \nAnseer below \n We have regions and in regions we have data center as you can see\n Az1 , Az2 ..... AZn zone . \n  \n DNS depenceing on the request will distribute request to near by \n regions \n\n\n\n \n\n ",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
